## DOMAIN 2: DESIGN SYSTEM & COLOR SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH
*(Authoritative Table: [`AGENTS.md` Section 2.10](file:///AGENTS.md#210-grade) & Detailed Tokens: [`.agents/rules/ui-invariants.md`](file:///.agents/rules/ui-invariants.md))*
11. SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH COLORING: Never hardcode grade colors. Reference CSS variables (`--grade-*`) and `TOPSCORE_COLORS` in `js/grading.js`.
- Star (★, 100%): Strictly **Electric Pink** (`#ff2d87`, dark slate `#0F172A` text, exclusive to Star).
- Palette: Grade A Pure Green (`#00c000ff`), B Electric Lime (`#95ff00ff`), C Pure Yellow (`#FFFF00`), D Dark Orange (`#FF8C00`), E Pure Red (`#FF0000`).
- Badges: Circular badges (`.grade-circle`) strictly render dark slate `#0F172A` text. Dynamic PTS follows `getGradeColorByScore()`.
26. UNIVERSAL SINGLE-SOURCE COLOR PROPAGATION ("RUBAH SATU MAKA RUBAH SEMUA") (/learn):
    - All Red elements follow Grade E (`--grade-e` / `var(--grade-e)` / `TOPSCORE_COLORS.E` / `.text-fail`).
    - All Yellow elements follow Grade C (`--grade-c` / `var(--grade-c)` / `TOPSCORE_COLORS.C` / `.text-warning`).
    - All Green elements follow Grade A (`--grade-a` / `var(--grade-a)` / `TOPSCORE_COLORS.A` / `.text-success`).
    - Star Pink (`#ff2d87`) remains 100% exclusive to Star 100%. System chrome uses neutral workstation tokens.
    - Zero raw hardcoded hex literals in CSS or JS. Any change to a central token in `:root` must instantaneously propagate across the entire application in a single step.

